        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a343f350-02a8-5c44-9402-dafe25c119be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference\n- People: Clement Attlee\n- Organizations: British Commonwealth, Labour Party\n- Places: United Kingdom\n- Roles: Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, Leader of the Labour Party\n\nFacts:\n- Clement Attlee was born on 3 January 1883.\n- The 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference was the third meeting of the heads of government of the British Commonwealth.\n- The 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference was held in the United Kingdom in October 1948.\n- Clement Attlee, Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, hosted the 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference.\n- Clement Attlee served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1945 to 1951.\n- Clement Attlee served as Leader of the Labour Party from 1935 to 1955.\n- Clement Attlee died on 8 October 1967.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "71f42eef-555e-5ad5-88c8-d84997fd268e",
        "text": "Page: 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference. Sentence: The 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference was the third Meeting of the Heads of Government of the British Commonwealth.\nPage: 1948 Commonwealth Prime Ministers' Conference. Sentence: It was held in the United Kingdom in October 1948, and was hosted by that country's Prime Minister, Clement Attlee.\nPage: Clement Attlee. Sentence: Clement Richard Attlee, 1st Earl Attlee, {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (3 January 1883 – 8 October 1967) was a British Labour politician who served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1945 to 1951 and Leader of the Labour Party from 1935 to 1955.",
